ixed label moments?', 'yes', 'current_code.py defines a=2.998 and b=1.092 outside its objective.'),\n('Does v32 already use pretrained transformer predictions?', 'yes', 'current_code.py averages DeBERTa checkpoint softmax outputs, loads oof.pkl, and merges fb3 predictions.'),\n('Does v32 explicitly align cached training rows to train.csv before positional feature assignment?', 'no', 'current_code.py loads train_df_30jun.pkl and immediately assigns n-grams and DeBERTa arrays positionally.'),\n('Are vectorized test rows labeled using their source CSV IDs?', 'no', \\\"current_code.py assigns df['essay_id'] = test_feats['essay_id'] after sorted feature aggregations.\\\"),\n('Does v32 merge transformer OOF features by essay ID?', 'no', 'oof.pkl is assigned column by column without IDs; the existing train.csv order convention cannot be verified without the artifact.'),\n('Does v32 fit a complementary squared-error LightGBM family?', 'no', 'Its active fold loop uses only objective=qwk_obj.'),\n('Does v32 save per-family OOF predictions?', 'no', 'No active OOF array persistence appears in current_code.py.'),\n('Does v32 use ordinary rounding for final scores?', 'yes', 'Final predictions are clipped to 1..6 then rounded.'),\n('Does v32 write the final scores by matching submission IDs?', 'no', \\\"current_code.py assigns submission['score']=predictions positionally.\\\"),\n('Does v32 rely on precomputed test feature data?', 'yes', 'It loads essay-scoring-features/df_test.pkl; cached coverage of rerun test IDs cannot be verified without data.'),\n]\nreport={'observations':[{'observation':q,'result':r,'evidence':e} for q,r,e in obs], 'action_summary':'Remove pre-CV topic downsampling and SMOTE, plus balanced regression weights, to recover natural score marginals and leakage-free base validation. Keep the existing checkpoints, feature pipeline and Kaggle paths; align rows by essay ID, preserve floating-point OOF, use fold-local QWK moments, and add compact transformer ordinal summaries. Train two seeds of five-fold QWK and squared-error LightGBM, cache models/OOF, and accept a small transformer/booster blend only when cross-fitted meta-validation improves; retain fixed rounding. Preserve the supplied anonymous OOF ordering assumption and cached feature dependency; no training or inference was run.'}\nPath('output/report.json').write_text(json.dumps(report,indent=2)+'\\\\n')\nPY\npython output/edit_revision.py\npython -m py_compile output/revised_code.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
